02:39:52.400 --> 02:39:54.686
work that is underway this year. As you can see in the roadmap, as we

02:39:55.186 --> 02:39:57.730
look forward to the future of this year and beyond, our progress and momentum continue

02:39:58.230 --> 02:40:00.830
to build. Now, I will give you a heads up. The presentation is lengthy,

02:40:01.330 --> 02:40:05.230
maybe a bit longer than we normally would bring to you,

02:40:05.470 --> 02:40:08.110
but for good reason.

02:40:08.270 --> 02:40:12.750
There's a lot of good information that we need to highlight and recap

02:40:13.250 --> 02:40:16.310
and to the Mayor's point, get the information out.

02:40:16.810 --> 02:40:20.350
And so please bear with us. We appreciate

02:40:20.850 --> 02:40:23.400
your focus as we get through this presentation today. We are going to cover in

02:40:23.900 --> 02:40:29.280
this presentation the status of the housing units and data insights over

02:40:29.780 --> 02:40:32.800
time, a summary of the work we advanced in 2025 and what we are working

02:40:33.300 --> 02:40:37.480
on now, the focus of our advocacy efforts,

02:40:37.980 --> 02:40:41.240
updates on grant funding,

02:40:42.040 --> 02:40:45.960
some of the challenges we will continue to face, and highlights from our communications

02:40:46.280 --> 02:40:48.280
and engagement efforts.

02:40:49.250 --> 02:40:52.650
There are many takeaways here, so I'd like to be deliberate in pointing three of

02:40:53.150 --> 02:40:59.090
them out for you. Guelph's housing ready progress is evident. We see this

02:40:59.590 --> 02:41:02.690
in the increasing housing units identified through development applications in 2025 compared to 2024.

