02:44:47.260 --> 02:44:50.780
As CAO Baker indicated in the

02:44:51.280 --> 02:44:55.660
introduction, the city is advancing five key strategies to meet

02:44:56.380 --> 02:44:59.260
housing demand and build sustainable communities.

02:44:59.340 --> 02:45:03.060
One such strategy is

02:45:03.560 --> 02:45:06.660
unlocking land for housing by advancing critical water, wastewater, transportation and transit

02:45:07.160 --> 02:45:10.860
infrastructure upgrades to remove servicing constraints and create new homes.

02:45:11.970 --> 02:45:15.650
We are also generating more development sites through the strategic disposal of unused city owned

02:45:16.150 --> 02:45:21.023
land. Looking back over the past year,

02:45:21.523 --> 02:45:24.050
here are some examples of how we delivered on this strategy. We sold at fair

02:45:24.210 --> 02:45:27.530
market value half an acre of unused city owned land to a private developer

02:45:28.030 --> 02:45:31.890
to build a future

02:45:32.290 --> 02:45:36.740
residential development with 57 units.

02:45:39.370 --> 02:45:42.810
We continue to advance housing readiness through

02:45:43.310 --> 02:45:47.130
several environmental assessments for downtown Claremont, Malpe and the Guelph Innovation District. We substantially

02:45:47.630 --> 02:45:49.930
completed $13.5 million worth of linear construction,

02:45:50.730 --> 02:45:54.170
2.5 which was funded through development charges, and this resulted in

02:45:54.670 --> 02:45:57.970
the construction of 6.2 metres of road, 0.3 kilometers

02:45:58.470 --> 02:46:02.170
of water main, 0.3 kilometers of sanitary and 0.3 kilometers of

02:46:02.670 --> 02:46:06.140
storm they're typically built together and one kilometer

02:46:06.640 --> 02:46:13.660
of cycling tracks or multi-use paths. We also started construction

02:46:14.160 --> 02:46:16.740
on projects in 2025 that we'll be completing this year. And a notable highlight is

02:46:17.240 --> 02:46:21.180
the $2 million street sewer upsized project on Wellington Street, which unlocked housing and

02:46:21.680 --> 02:46:24.860
development. And you had one of those housing applications before you earlier this morning,

02:46:25.360 --> 02:46:28.695
which is a direct result of that Wellington street construction that occurred last

02:46:29.195 --> 02:46:33.110
year. So the city is also now available to offer financial agreement opportunities for

02:46:33.610 --> 02:46:36.990
key infrastructure to remove servicing constraints and unlock

02:46:37.490 --> 02:46:40.990
capacity for new homes through the launch

02:46:41.630 --> 02:46:45.430
of what we call the municipal financing servicing and financing agreements,

02:46:45.930 --> 02:46:49.510
but that's also known as the front-end

02:46:50.010 --> 02:46:53.430
agreement that was put forward. So we found ways to increase budget

02:46:53.930 --> 02:46:55.447
certainty speed up timelines for developers and we also made investments to improve our transit

02:46:56.490 --> 02:47:00.060
unlock servicing capacity for 27, 000. And residents. And both projects have open houses

02:47:00.560 --> 02:47:04.100
planned for the spring and there are web pages on

02:47:04.600 --> 02:47:07.260
those projects. For the Guelph Innovation District, which we also talked about earlier,

02:47:07.620 --> 02:47:11.260
last summer the Victoria Road, Stone Road and McQuillin's Bridge Municipal

02:47:11.760 --> 02:47:14.060
Class EA started and the study team is looking for options on that which we

02:47:14.560 --> 02:47:17.940
will be bringing forward. We also have improvements to Stone Road,

02:47:18.100 --> 02:47:21.830
which are planned for detailed design in 2023 and construction in 2031. Other growth

02:47:22.070 --> 02:47:25.390
infrastructure, York Road phase four, I know we've had lots

02:47:25.890 --> 02:47:28.790
of talks about York Road,

02:47:29.290 --> 02:47:33.710
but its construction continues in 2026. Exhibition Park neighbourhood area phase

02:47:34.210 --> 02:47:37.790
one starts this year and the Hanlan Sanitary and Watermain

02:47:38.290 --> 02:47:42.910
Crossing detailed trunk design starts this year as well. University Avenue

02:47:43.410 --> 02:47:47.790
West construction starts later this

02:47:48.290 --> 02:47:51.710
year, and we also note 87,000 new transit service

02:47:51.790 --> 02:47:59.190
areas will be added between 2026 and 2031 subject to our annual budget

02:47:59.690 --> 02:48:03.950
process. Our second strategy is that we're enabling greater density through

02:48:04.450 --> 02:48:09.110
new policies and programs that make it easier and more affordable to build housing

02:48:09.610 --> 02:48:12.630
while keep growth aligned with our

02:48:13.130 --> 02:48:17.070
community priorities. In December, you'll recall Council

02:48:17.570 --> 02:48:20.870
approved an amendment to our ADU grant program

02:48:21.370 --> 02:48:24.990
as part of the affordable housing community improvement plan,

02:48:25.550 --> 02:48:31.470
which unlocked additional potential, increased funding and eligibility

02:48:31.970 --> 02:48:36.070
amounts. The grant program so far has incented 15 affordable units all

02:48:36.570 --> 02:48:43.480
under the homeowner stream. Another key highlight of of

02:48:43.980 --> 02:48:48.160
the CIP is the $320,000

02:48:48.660 --> 02:48:52.080
which was awarded to Wyndham House through the City's Affordable

02:48:52.580 --> 02:48:55.960
Housing CIP Vacant Unit Renewal Grant.

02:48:56.600 --> 02:49:00.000
And this was for 10 youth spaces on Waterloo Avenue. And with

02:49:00.500 --> 02:49:04.640
the new supportive housing development, this puts Guelph on track to become

02:49:05.140 --> 02:49:08.290
the first mid-sized city in Canada to end chronic youth homelessness. Last April, we approved

02:49:09.730 --> 02:49:13.330
the Official Plan

02:49:13.830 --> 02:49:17.450
Amendment 106 that allows taller buildings in the downtown secondary plan area to meet

02:49:17.950 --> 02:49:21.809
our population and employment growth

02:49:22.309 --> 02:49:26.090
to 2051. We will also be bringing forward

02:49:26.590 --> 02:49:31.570
the downtown community planning permit system next

02:49:31.650 --> 02:49:35.830
month for council's decision. The CPPS will be brought forward next

02:49:36.330 --> 02:49:39.670
month and then with that we'll also be bringing later this

02:49:40.170 --> 02:49:44.110
year the accompanying built form standards to talk about height and have

02:49:48.670 --> 02:49:51.870
a citywide standard on what that looks like so we can increase the

02:49:52.370 --> 02:49:55.070
clarity and certainty for developers for what we're looking on housing as it comes forward.

02:49:55.570 --> 02:49:59.150
Grant funding is still available through the city's affordable housing

02:50:01.330 --> 02:50:05.290
Community Improvement Plan and staff are continuing to work with

02:50:05.790 --> 02:50:09.650
interested parties in the affordable housing development space and

02:50:09.810 --> 02:50:13.631
encourage other housing nonprofits, builders and

02:50:14.131 --> 02:50:16.450
residents to apply and we continue on our outreach and communication for that program.

02:50:16.610 --> 02:50:19.970
Our third strategy is what we're calling reducing barriers

02:50:20.210 --> 02:50:24.090
for developers and property owners by improving processes,

02:50:24.590 --> 02:50:28.870
shortening timelines, increasing flexibility

02:50:29.270 --> 02:50:32.790
in land uses and creating clearer, more predictable development

02:50:33.290 --> 02:50:36.750
pathways. Last year, our Building Services team enhanced their services

02:50:37.250 --> 02:50:40.950
to better support the segment of customers calling

02:50:41.450 --> 02:50:44.830
for building permit applications assistance and for assistance remotely. Through the

02:50:45.330 --> 02:50:46.590
use of an app, customers can now share their screen with staff and together walk

02:50:47.090 --> 02:50:50.630
through each step in the application process from the comfort of their home.

02:50:53.040 --> 02:50:57.120
We also undertook a Lean Yellow Belt continuous improvement project to

02:50:57.280 --> 02:51:01.180
increase the number of complete additional dwelling unit permit applications. Through their hard work

02:51:01.680 --> 02:51:04.640
of staff, they reduced incomplete ADU permits by 33% and allowed ADU permits to come

02:51:05.760 --> 02:51:09.000
in much easier and quicker for the applicants. Last April,

02:51:09.500 --> 02:51:17.730
this council approved the Stone and Edinburgh Road community

02:51:18.230 --> 02:51:22.010
planning permit system. So we're trying

02:51:22.090 --> 02:51:25.610
to bring a bunch of processes together, site plan, official plan amendment,

02:51:26.110 --> 02:51:30.050
zoning, minor variants all into one

02:51:30.550 --> 02:51:33.590
45 day process. And as we talk, we do have two applications that are in

02:51:34.090 --> 02:51:36.830
the pre-consultation stage in that area. So that's great news and the program is exciting

02:51:37.330 --> 02:51:40.930
for both those applicants. Planning has also started our

02:51:41.430 --> 02:51:44.730
multi-phased official plan amendment Updates phase

02:51:45.130 --> 02:51:48.330
one, which was presented to council in February, included provincial changes to the Planning Act,

02:51:48.830 --> 02:51:52.210
the Ontario Heritage Act, and the new provincial planning statement.

02:51:52.710 --> 02:51:56.650
Phase two is underway, which is to be presented to council for approval in

02:51:57.150 --> 02:52:02.690
2027, and it focuses on

02:52:03.190 --> 02:52:06.610
employment, transportation, and will include an interim employment land strategy

02:52:07.110 --> 02:52:09.860
because of changes to the definition by the province.

02:52:10.170 --> 02:52:13.250
As was approved last month,

02:52:13.750 --> 02:52:17.810
WELF will apply

02:52:18.310 --> 02:52:22.330
additional rigor in tracking our servicing allocation to proactively manage the city's

02:52:22.830 --> 02:52:25.850
unallocated water and wastewater servicing capacity. Last week,

02:52:25.929 --> 02:52:29.050
staff brought forward to council the DC

02:52:29.550 --> 02:52:33.850
updates that outlined regulatory changes and a call to action on

02:52:34.350 --> 02:52:38.180
other levels of government to to help fund the gap. And last month,

02:52:38.680 --> 02:52:42.460
we also approved the citywide terms of reference for the parking study.

02:52:42.960 --> 02:52:46.500
Bill 185 enables municipalities to impose lapsing provisions on site plans and

02:52:47.000 --> 02:52:51.060
draft plans. If a building permit is not issued

02:52:51.540 --> 02:52:54.980
within a prescribed period of time, we have been doing this for plans

02:52:55.480 --> 02:52:59.740
of subdivision as it was previously approved.

02:53:00.240 --> 02:53:01.300
But we are going to be doing it for site plans as well to encourage

02:53:01.550 --> 02:53:04.950
developers to move quickly through the process and that is

02:53:05.450 --> 02:53:08.430
coming forward to council next month.

02:53:09.390 --> 02:53:13.430
Our fourth strategy is that we're streamlining reviews and approvals

02:53:13.930 --> 02:53:17.950
by digitizing our processes, improving transparency and strengthening collaboration resulting in faster,

02:53:18.450 --> 02:53:21.950
more efficient housing delivery. As part of our half action

02:53:24.590 --> 02:53:28.350
plan initiative number two,

02:53:28.740 --> 02:53:32.420
We committed to a series of milestones that will support

02:53:33.140 --> 02:53:36.660
and streamline development and the construction of new housing.

02:53:37.160 --> 02:53:40.900
To realise this, the Planning Services team and the IT department

02:53:41.400 --> 02:53:44.140
hired an outside consultant to review our work, to review our process workflows. And we

02:53:44.640 --> 02:53:48.500
worked together to complete a broad review of our development processes, I think

02:53:49.000 --> 02:53:52.420
for the third time since I've been here, but the results is a roadmap for

02:53:52.920 --> 02:53:56.670
making better use of our technology and and

02:53:57.170 --> 02:54:00.470
expanding our digital services in a

02:54:00.970 --> 02:54:05.310
streamlined development review process. So the city's planning

02:54:05.810 --> 02:54:12.690
and IT teams are working together on

02:54:13.190 --> 02:54:17.510
how we can use our existing technologies as they relate to

02:54:18.010 --> 02:54:20.310
development processes. And this will be completed in Q2 2026 with a primary focus on

02:54:20.810 --> 02:54:22.690
customer needs, allowing for a IT solution versus a paper solution. Where applicants can track

02:54:23.330 --> 02:54:27.170
their progress in the development approval process. They can pay their fees online

02:54:27.670 --> 02:54:31.410
and everything can move to

02:54:31.910 --> 02:54:35.530
a digital system from the paper process we

02:54:36.030 --> 02:54:40.330
currently have. So again, we're trying to make it easier and quicker for

02:54:40.830 --> 02:54:45.130
developers to work within the city. Through our city's development advisor,

02:54:45.630 --> 02:54:49.050
we are proactively engaging the development community and identifying pain

02:54:49.550 --> 02:54:50.330
points and the development advisor is working on those pain points to improve the processes

02:54:50.810 --> 02:54:53.930
and identify those key relationships with our interest holders.

02:54:56.970 --> 02:55:00.770
The other thing to note is last year in the planning department

02:55:01.270 --> 02:55:06.090
we reorganised our structure and created a dedicated

02:55:06.590 --> 02:55:12.010
site plan team to get to that last

02:55:12.510 --> 02:55:16.010
mile, to get that last step, to ensure that developers can move quickly from an

02:55:16.510 --> 02:55:20.090
early site plan process to a building permit, which would get

02:55:20.590 --> 02:55:23.570
shovels in the ground quicker.

02:55:24.070 --> 02:55:28.090
And we are seeing through that site

02:55:28.590 --> 02:55:31.930
plan stage that that is working. So in Q2,

02:55:32.430 --> 02:55:36.450
council will be receiving also recommendations

02:55:36.950 --> 02:55:40.410
for the value for money audit

02:55:40.910 --> 02:55:45.110
of the building permit process inspections and that was part of the

02:55:45.610 --> 02:55:49.590
council's audit plan. So again, we're continuing to look

02:55:50.090 --> 02:55:53.710
at our processes and see how we can do things better and if

02:55:54.210 --> 02:55:57.150
there's any areas gaps that can be found. So with that,

02:55:57.710 --> 02:56:01.030
now I will turn it over to

02:56:01.530 --> 02:56:07.310
Kushla Matthews, the City's Manager of

02:56:07.390 --> 02:56:10.760
Community and Affordable Housing. Great. Thank you

02:56:11.260 --> 02:56:14.880
very much, Ms. Walkie. So our fifth and final strategy

